<title>USA: U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Cash bids falter.</title>
<headline>U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Cash bids falter.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dark northern spring wheat bids faltered Monday, with some of the weakness stemming from weakness in basis levels, dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;Both basis and futures got hit pretty hard today,&quot; one Montana dealer said. &quot;I know there's a lot of wheat that traded out in the country on last week's rallies, so that's partly why.&quot;</p>
<p>MGE spring wheat futures lost ground Monday on spillover bearishness from CBOT and KCBT wheat, dealers said.</p>
<p>March wheat on the MGE closed down 7-1/4 cents per bushel at $3.74-1/4, and May lost 3-1/4 to close at $3.60-1/2.  </p>
